1: # Technical Investigation & Design Report: Google TV Cinema Scrub Bar (Milestone UI-M3)
2: 
3: **Author**: Explorer 1 (`explorer_ui_m3_1`)  
4: **Role**: Player HUD & Cinema Scrub Bar Explorer  
5: **Date**: 2026-11-05  
6: **Target Platform**: LG webOS 8.5.0 / LG 32LR686BPSA (1920x1080 10-Foot Television Canvas)  
7: **Assigned Working Directory**: `/home/prem/webos-projects/cinejoy-webos/.agents/teamwork/explorer_ui_m3_1/`
8: 
9: ---
10: 
11: ## 1. Executive Summary
12: 
13: Milestone UI-M3 modernizes the CineJoy LG webOS Media Player Heads-Up Display (HUD) overlay and timeline scrub bar to reflect Google TV / cinema-grade design language (`theboringtv-lgwebos` reference design), while preserving 100% of underlying playback pipelines, spatial D-pad navigation, and test contracts.
14: 
15: Explorer 1 was tasked with investigating `app/js/player.js`, `app/css/components.css`, `app/index.html`, and related test suites (`app/test-m5.js`, `tests/adversarial-m5-osd-remote.js`, `tests/adversarial-m5-stress.js`, `tests/run-all-tests.js`) to produce an actionable engineering design for:
16: 1. **Google TV Cinema Scrub Bar**: Slender progress track with elapsed time (`#e8eaed`, Google Sans), buffered range visualization, and remaining time display (`-HH:MM:SS` in `#bdc1c6`).
17: 2. **Visual & Spatial Dimensions**: 8px resting track expanding to 12px on spatial focus, high-contrast 24px thumb with 5px white halo ring + neon lime glow, and smooth cubic-bezier transitions.
18: 3. **Seeking Visual Feedback Toast (±15s)**: Translucent dark glass pill toast (`rgba(14, 16, 20, 0.92)`), Google TV typography, pure DOM SVG icon construction, and seek delta synchronization.
19: 4. **Autonomous 4000ms Idle Auto-Hide Timer**: Full preservation of 4000ms countdown, permanent suspension on playback pause and active modals, boundary resets (3950ms–4050ms), and immediate HUD wakeup on remote input.
20: 5. **Zero DOM Sinks Compliance**: Elimination of all `.innerHTML =` sinks in `player.js` (play icon, seek feedback icon, modal list builders) in favor of pure W3C DOM node APIs (`createElementNS`, `setAttribute`, `appendChild`).
21: 6. **Strict DOM ID Preservation**: Complete retention of all 40+ existing DOM IDs and event bindings to prevent regressions across 773 test checks.
