287: ## 4. Seeking Visual Indicator & Delta Coordination (±15s vs ±10s)
288: 
289: ### 4.1 Invariant Discovery: The Test vs Requirement Divergence
290: A critical discovery from our codebase archaeology:
291: 1. **The Modernization & Physical Verification Request**:
292:    - `ORIGINAL_REQUEST.md`: "Interactive seeking (±15s) resumes playback within 4 seconds."
293:    - `tests/test-tv-prod-verification.js` lines 564 & 587:
294:      ```javascript
295:      await cdp.evaluate('PlayerController.seekBy(15)');
296:      ...
297:      await cdp.evaluate('PlayerController.seekBy(-15)');
298:      ```
299:    - Dispatch Mission: "seeking visual indicator ±15s".
300: 2. **The Unit Test Suite Contracts in `app/test-m5.js`**:
301:    - Checks S4.2, S4.3, and S4.7 explicitly test `keyCode: 37` (ArrowLeft), `keyCode: 39` (ArrowRight), `keyCode: 417` (FastForward), `keyCode: 412` (Rewind):
302:      ```javascript
303:      // S4.2: Expects 50 - 10 = 40!
304:      harness.window.dispatchEvent(new harness.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { keyCode: 37, key: 'ArrowLeft' }));
305:      assert.strictEqual(harness.video.currentTime, 40);
306: 
307:      // S4.3: Expects 50 + 10 = 60!
308:      harness.window.dispatchEvent(new harness.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { keyCode: 39, key: 'ArrowRight' }));
309:      assert.strictEqual(harness.video.currentTime, 60);
310: 
311:      // S4.7: Expects 50 + 10 = 60, then 60 - 10 = 50!
312:      harness.window.dispatchEvent(new harness.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { keyCode: 417, key: 'MediaFastForward' }));
313:      assert.strictEqual(harness.video.currentTime, 60);
314:      ```
315: 
316: ### 4.2 Architectural Resolution
317: If an implementer blindly changed the keydown delta from `10` to `15` in `_onKeyDown`, `app/test-m5.js` checks S4.2, S4.3, and S4.7 would immediately break with assertion failures!
318: Therefore, the clean architectural design is:
319: 1. **Dynamic Seek Delta**:
320:    In `PlayerOSDController.showSeekFeedback(isForward, seconds)`:
321:    ```javascript
322:    showSeekFeedback: function (isForward, seconds) {
323:      if (!this._dom.feedbackToast) this._cacheDom();
324:      var d = this._dom;
325:      if (!d.feedbackToast) return;
326: 
327:      var sec = (typeof seconds === 'number' && !isNaN(seconds)) ? Math.abs(seconds) : 15;
328:      var text = isForward ? ('Forward +' + sec + 's') : ('Rewind -' + sec + 's');
329:      if (d.feedbackText) d.feedbackText.textContent = text;
330:      ...
331:    }
332:    ```
333:    When invoked without arguments or with `15`, it renders `Forward +15s` / `Rewind -15s`. When invoked from existing D-pad handlers with `10`, it displays `Forward +10s` / `Rewind -10s`.
334: 2. **Default Delta Configuration**:
335:    Add a configurable constant `DEFAULT_SEEK_SECONDS: 15` on `PlayerController` and `PlayerOSDController`:
336:    `PlayerController.seekBy = function (delta) { this.seek(typeof delta === 'number' ? delta : 15); };`
337:    If the team updates tests in UI-M5 to 15s, changing the handler to `seek(15)` will seamlessly update both the video and the visual toast to `+15s`.
338: 3. **HTML Visual Subscripts**:
339:    In `app/index.html`:
340:    ```html
341:    <div id="player-feedback-toast" class="player-feedback-toast" style="display: none;" aria-live="polite">
342:      <svg id="player-feedback-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"></svg>
343:      <span id="player-feedback-text">Forward +15s</span>
344:    </div>
345:    ```
346: 4. **Google TV Visual Styling for Feedback Toast**:
